# --- Dependencies & build output ---
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.vite/

# --- Secrets ---
# The TMDB key lives here; .env.example is the committed template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Runtime state (never commit) ---
# `data/` holds the imported catalogue and everything the server persists.
#
# This matters more than it looks: provider stream URLs embed the subscription's
# username and password (".../movie/<user>/<pass>/<id>.mkv"), so vod.json and
# channels.json are credentials in bulk. users.json and admin.json carry PIN and
# password hashes, sessions.json carries live session tokens, and metadata.db
# runs to hundreds of megabytes — past what GitHub accepts in a single file.
#
# Patterns are unanchored (no leading slash) so they apply at every level:
# `server/data/…` as well as `./data/…`. The previous `data/*.json` had a slash
# in the middle, which git anchors to the repository root — so nothing under
# server/data was actually ignored.
# `**/` keeps this unanchored, and excluding the *contents* rather than the
# directory is what lets .gitkeep be re-included — git never looks inside a
# directory it has excluded outright.
**/data/*
!**/data/.gitkeep
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
storage/

# --- Local tooling ---
# Claude Code's local settings record the exact commands that were approved,
# which in this project included curl calls carrying the provider password.
.claude/

# --- OS / editor noise ---
.DS_Store
*.log
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
